at="intermediate"><addressbook><name>APPLIED MATERIALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARIMA, SEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARIMURA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, YOUJI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARIMA SEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARIMURA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI YOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARIMA, SEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARIMURA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, YOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An epitaxial growth apparatus includes a processing chamber composed of fused silica, and a wafer support arranged in the processing chamber. Halogen lamps are arranged above and below the processing chamber to heat a semiconductor wafer supported on the wafer support. The wafer support includes a susceptor for holding the wafer and a susceptor support shaft for supporting the susceptor on the lower side. Arms are extended radially from the main shaft of the susceptor support shaft to support the susceptor at three points. Since no projection for support is present under the center of the susceptor, the heat from the lower halogen lamps is not interrupted and the semiconductor wafer can be heated uniformly.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un appareil de croissance épitaxiale qui comporte une chambre de traitement constituée de silice fondue, et un support de plaquette placé dans la chambre de traitement. Des lampes halogènes sont disposées au-dessus et au-dessous de la chambre de traitement, de sorte qu'une plaquette en semi-conducteur supportée par le support de plaquette soit chauffé. Le support de plaquette comporte un suscepteur qui porte la plaquette et un arbre de support de suscepteur qui soutient le suscepteur sur son côté inférieur. Des bras s'étendent radialement depuis l'arbre principal de l'arbre de support du suscepteur, de sorte que le suscepteur soit soutenu en trois points. Etant donné qu'aucun support n'est prévu au-dessous du centre du suscepteur, la chaleur en provenance des lampes halogènes inférieures n'est pas interrompue et la plaquette en semi-conducteur peut être chauffée de manière homogène.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>